53"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2019-11-29","study_type":"article","title":"Microplastic (1 and 5 \u03bcm) exposure disturbs lifespan and intestine function in the nematode Caenorhabditis elegans","type":"article","work_id":"W2991599663","year":2019},{"abstract":"","author_ids":["A5011805813","A5039537374","A5059622174","A5080078616","A5100370653","A5100717842","A5100737340","A5102558216","A5108062674","A5112381117"],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":80,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2020.124132","domain_tags":["analytical_methods","fate_transport_and_sorption"],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I27781120","I4210109544","I55712492","I84218800"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Journal of Hazardous Materials","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2020.124132","openalex_topics":["T10419","T10753","T14106"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2020-09-29","study_type":"article","title":"Transport and fate of microplastics from riverine sediment dredge piles: Implications for disposal","type":"article","work_id":"W3091186399","year":2020},{"abstract":"","author_ids":["A5009445894","A5011805813","A5013001872","A5039537374","A5080865186","A5102558216","A5103524090","A5103876693","A5103969144","A5108062674","A5110370164"],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":471,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2021.126007","domain_tags":["air"],"facet_tags":["matrix:air","matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I146620803","I27781120","I4210109544","I84218800"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Journal of Hazardous Materials","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2021.126007","openalex_topics":["T10122","T10419","T10753"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2021-05-06","study_type":"article","title":"Airborne microplastics in indoor and outdoor environments of a coastal city in Eastern China","type":"article","work_id":"W3157988795","year":2021},{"abstract":"Airborne microplastics (MPs) are receiving increasing attention due to their ubiquitous nature and the potential human health consequences resulting from inhalation. The limited data for airborne MP concentrations vary widely among studies (\u223c4 orders of magnitude), but comparisons are tenuous due to the inconsistent collection and detection/enumeration methodologies among studies. Herein, we used uniform methodologies to obtain comparable airborne MP concentration data to assess MP exposure intensity in five Chinese megacities. Airborne MP concentrations in northern cities (358 \u00b1 132 items/m 3 ) were higher than those in southeast cities (230 \u00b1 94 items/m 3 ) but of a similar order of magnitude, unlike previous studies. The majority (94.7%) of MPs found in air samples were smaller than 100 \u03bcm, and the main shape of airborne MPs was fragments (88.2%). Polyethylene, polyester, and polystyrene were the dominant polymers comprising airborne MPs. No consistent relationships were detected between airborne MP concentration and typical socioeconomic indices, and the spatial and diurnal patterns for airborne MPs were different from various components of air quality indices (PM 2.5, PM 10, etc.). These findings reflect the contrasting source/generation dynamics between airborne MPs and other airborne pollutants. Maximum annual exposure of humans to airborne MPs was estimated in the range of 1\u20132 million/year in these megacities, highlighting the need for additional research examining the human health risks from the inhalation of airborne MPs.","author_ids":["A5009445894","A5013001872","A5039537374","A5042048214","A5062239873","A5080865186","A5100548443","A5100747998","A5103969144","A5108062674","A5109756687","A5110802105"],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":194,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.est.1c03618","domain_tags":["air","human_exposure_and_health_risk","risk_assessment"],"facet_tags":["matrix:air"],"institution_ids":["I211433327","I27781120","I4210109544","I84218800"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Environmental Science & Technology","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"green","oa_url":"https://escholarship.org/content/qt6vf7v59s/qt6vf7v59s.pdf","openalex_topics":["T10122","T10419","T10753"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2021-09-24","study_type":"article","title":"Airborne Microplastic Concentrations in Five Megacities of Northern and Southeast China","type":"article","work_id":"W3199762035","year":2021},{"abstract":"","author_ids":["A5009445894","A5011805813","A5013001872","A5039537374","A5040992255","A5042048214","A5100370653","A5100717842","A5100737340","A5103969144","A5108062674","A5109756687"],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":118,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2022.128674","domain_tags":["air","ecotoxicology_and_trophic_transfer","human_exposure_and_health_risk"],"facet_tags":["matrix:air"],"institution_ids":["I27781120","I84218800"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Journal of Hazardous Materials","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"green","oa_url":"https://escholarship.org/content/qt4rh61290/qt4rh61290.pdf?t=r9kba8","openalex_topics":["T10122","T10419","T10753"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2022-03-11","study_type":"article","title":"Microplastic ingestion from atmospheric deposition during dining/drinking activities","type":"article","work_id":"W4220760495","year":2022},{"abstract":"","author_ids":["A5011805813","A5039537374","A5069464955","A5100370653","A5100411478","A5100717842","A5100737340","A510155